  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "constructor-validation-before-create",
      "evidence": "texture-constructor.il lines1\u201347, IL_0001\u2013IL_004c; direct-dependencies.il Texture::.ctor; validation-dependencies.il Object::.ctor",
      "finding": "Six-argument constructor first forwards to Texture::.ctor then Object::.ctor and opaque System.Object::.ctor. It calls ValidateFormat(format). False branches directly to final ret without format mapping, crunch testing or Internal_Create; normal managed constructor return is not proof of native texture creation or usable atlas. True maps format with !linear, uses numeric flag0 when mipCount==1 else1, ORs64 for IsCrunchFormat, then forwards this,width,height,mipCount,mapped graphics format,flags,nativeTex unchanged to Internal_Create. IsCrunchFormat matches numeric TextureFormat28/29/64/65. No enum-name interpretation or live parameter value was inferred."
    },
    {
      "id": "support-and-decompression-branch",
      "evidence": "direct-dependencies.il ValidateFormat/GetGraphicsFormat; validation-dependencies.il SupportsTextureFormat/CanDecompressFormat; leaf-dependencies.il",
      "finding": "SupportsTextureFormat boxes the TextureFormat and calls IsValidEnumValue. IsValidEnumValue uses opaque GetType and Enum.IsDefined; false leads to ArgumentException before SupportsTextureFormatNative. A supported native result returns true. Otherwise ValidateFormat tests native IsCompressedTextureFormat; only if compressed does it map format with boolean false and test CanDecompressFormat. That overload forwards boolean true to the native two-argument function. A true decompression result also returns true. Support/compression/mapping/decompression outputs and enum/BCL semantics were not executed; no actual platform/format acceptance inferred."
    },
    {
      "id": "unsupported-format-log-before-false",
      "evidence": "direct-dependencies.il ValidateFormat IL_0030\u2013IL_0054; validation-dependencies.il Debug.LogError; reused-dependencies.json and retained phase111 source trace",
      "finding": "When both support and decompression routes fail, ValidateFormat converts format via constrained Object.ToString, formats its literal diagnostic through opaque String.Format, then LogError(message,this), finally returns false only if those calls return. Exact new LogError wrapper fetches unityLogger, passes numeric severity0 and supplied context to ILogger.Log. Getter/interface declaration reuse verified phase110; phase111 default Logger/handler/filter dispatch reused conditionally. Unchanged default enabled=true/filter3 permits0, but current receiver/settings/writers are not observed. Conversion, formatting, interface/native logging can fail/reenter before false; filtering may suppress output. No unconditional diagnostic output or actual callback claimed."
    },
    {
      "id": "native-create-failure-no-local-rollback",
      "evidence": "direct-dependencies.il Internal_Create; validation-dependencies.il Internal_CreateImpl and UnityException::.ctor",
      "finding": "Internal_Create forwards seven arguments to Internal_CreateImpl, a private static InternalCall with no managed body. False constructs UnityException with exact invalid-parameters message then throws; true returns. UnityException forwards message to opaque SystemException::.ctor then calls opaque Exception.set_HResult(-2147467261). Native code may have effects before returning/failing; none observed. These selected methods have no local rollback/catch/locks/delegate Invoke or direct field stores. Dimensions/mipcount/native-pointer validity, allocation, native changes and callback behavior remain native/runtime boundaries, not validated outcomes."
    },
    {
      "id": "retained-state-and-gates",
      "evidence": "retained-input-verification.json; previous-checkpoint.json; phase111 source-trace hash",
      "finding": "Retain previous atlas caller ordering, font definition/synthesis/legacy/feature and logger results by hash. Feature logging precedes feature stores; legacy version1.1.0 precedes name/log; current/partial-state aliases/failures remain unexecuted. Do not infer renderer feasibility or accepted live source selection from managed construction. GlyphRect implicit initializer/current zero and TMP_Character forwarded base/unicode/glyphIndex/scale remain separately unread. All previously open controller/DB/Lua/save/callback/reachability/serialized/native/resource and final acceptance limits retained."
    }
  ],
